<div id="S2.Thmtheorem9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 2.9</span></span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmtheorem9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S2.Thmtheorem9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{1},\ldots,H_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{1},\ldots,H_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> be connected components of a <math id="S2.Thmtheorem9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> graph
<math id="S2.Thmtheorem9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S2.Thmtheorem9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\neq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\neq 2</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="S2.Thmtheorem9.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S2.Thmtheorem9.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-quasi-regularizable if and only if
<math id="S2.Thmtheorem9.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n(H_{i})\geq(p+1)\cdot\alpha(H_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n(H_{i})\geq(p+1)\cdot\alpha(H_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S2.Thmtheorem9.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq s</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.p61" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.p61.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p61.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof.</span> Let <math id="S2.p61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> be an independent set of <math id="S2.p61.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>. For each <math id="S2.p61.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq s</annotation></semantics></math>, define
<math id="S2.p61.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{i}=S\cap V(H_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{i}=S\cap V(H_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S2.p61.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> is independent in <math id="S2.p61.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>, each <math id="S2.p61.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is an
independent set in <math id="S2.p61.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. By Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem8" title="Theorem 2.8 ‣ 2 Quasi-regularizability of 𝐖_𝑝 graphs ‣ Log-concavity of the independence polynomials of 𝐖_𝑝 graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.8</span></a>, we have <math id="S2.p61.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|N_{H_{i}}(S_{i})\right|\geq p\cdot|S_{i}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|N_{H_{i}}(S_{i})\right|\geq p\cdot|S_{i}|</annotation></semantics></math>. Summing over all <math id="S2.p61.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, it
follows that</p>
<table id="S2.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|N_{G}(S)\right|=\sum_{i=1}^{s}\left|N_{H_{i}}(S_{i})\right|\geq\sum_{i=1}^{s}p\cdot\left|S_{i}\right|=p\cdot\sum_{i=1}^{s}\left|S_{i}\right|=p\cdot|S|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≥</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.055em">⋅</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>s</mi></munderover><mrow><mo>|</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|N_{G}(S)\right|=\sum_{i=1}^{s}\left|N_{H_{i}}(S_{i})\right|\geq\sum_{i=1}^{s}p\cdot\left|S_{i}\right|=p\cdot\sum_{i=1}^{s}\left|S_{i}\right|=p\cdot|S|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p61.2" class="ltx_p">Conversely, for each <math id="S2.p61.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq s</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S2.p61.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> be an independent set of
<math id="S2.p61.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S2.p61.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{H_{i}}(S_{i})=N_{G}(S_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{H_{i}}(S_{i})=N_{G}(S_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>, the assumption implies that
<math id="S2.p61.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|N_{H_{i}}(S_{i})\right|\geq p\cdot|S_{i}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|N_{H_{i}}(S_{i})\right|\geq p\cdot|S_{i}|</annotation></semantics></math>. Applying Theorem
<a href="#S2.Thmtheorem8" title="Theorem 2.8 ‣ 2 Quasi-regularizability of 𝐖_𝑝 graphs ‣ Log-concavity of the independence polynomials of 𝐖_𝑝 graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.8</span></a> again, we conclude that <math id="S2.p61.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n(H_{i})\geq(p+1)\cdot\alpha(H_{i})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n(H_{i})\geq(p+1)\cdot\alpha(H_{i}).</annotation></semantics></math>
 <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:5.0pt;height:5.0pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span>Log-concavity of independence polynomials of <math id="S3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> graphs</h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, the log-concavity problem is deeply concerned.
Let us recall some significant inequalities involving the coefficients of the
independent polynomial of a graph, for a later use.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3.1</span></span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">[</span><a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a><span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, Lemma 1]</span></cite><span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">  If <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(G;x)=\sum\limits_{k=0}^{\alpha\left(G\right)}s_{k}x^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(G;x)=\sum\limits_{k=0}^{\alpha\left(G\right)}s_{k}x^{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\left(G\right)\cdot s_{\alpha\left(G\right)}\leq n\cdot s_{\alpha\left(G\right)-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\left(G\right)\cdot s_{\alpha\left(G\right)}\leq n\cdot s_{\alpha\left(G\right)-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The following lemma serves as an efficient tool that enables us to prove the
main theorem.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3.2</span></span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(G;x)=\sum\limits_{k=0}^{\alpha\left(G\right)}s_{k}x^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(G;x)=\sum\limits_{k=0}^{\alpha\left(G\right)}s_{k}x^{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the following assertions are true:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S3.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><span id="S3.I1.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">[</span><a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a><span id="S3.I1.ix1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, Theorem 2.1]</span></cite><span id="S3.I1.ix1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> if </span><math id="S3.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.ix1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is </span><math id="S3.I1.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.ix1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-quasi-regularizable,
then</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(k+1)\cdot s_{k+1}\leq(n\left(G\right)-(\lambda+1)\cdot k)\cdot s_{k}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(k+1)\cdot s_{k+1}\leq(n\left(G\right)-(\lambda+1)\cdot k)\cdot s_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.I1.ix1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.ix1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for all </span><math id="S3.I1.ix1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq k\leq\alpha\left(G\right)-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq k\leq\alpha\left(G\right)-1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.ix1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">;</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><span id="S3.I1.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">[</span><a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a><span id="S3.I1.ix2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, Theorem 2.6]</span></cite><span id="S3.I1.ix2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> if </span><math id="S3.I1.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.ix2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is a connected graph in
</span><math id="S3.I1.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}_{p}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.ix2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\cdot(\alpha\left(G\right)-k)\cdot s_{k}\leq(k+1)\cdot s_{k+1}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\cdot(\alpha\left(G\right)-k)\cdot s_{k}\leq(k+1)\cdot s_{k+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.I1.ix2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.ix2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for all </span><math id="S3.I1.ix2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq k\leq\alpha\left(G\right)-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq k\leq\alpha\left(G\right)-1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.ix2.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3.3</span></span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> be a connected <math id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> graph with <math id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\neq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\neq 2</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=n(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=n(G)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=\alpha(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=\alpha(G)</annotation></semantics></math>. If</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{\alpha^{2}}{4\left(\alpha+1\right)}\leq p\text{ and }n\in\left[(p+1)\cdot\alpha,p\cdot\alpha+2\sqrt{p\cdot\alpha+p}\right]\text{ \ \ \ }" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> and </mtext><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>]</mo></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> </mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\alpha^{2}}{4\left(\alpha+1\right)}\leq p\text{ and }n\in\left[(p+1)\cdot\alpha,p\cdot\alpha+2\sqrt{p\cdot\alpha+p}\right]\text{ \ \ \ }</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">or</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{\alpha\left(\alpha-1\right)}{\alpha+1}\leq p\text{ and }n\in\left(p\cdot\alpha+2\sqrt{p\cdot\alpha+p},\frac{\allowbreak\left(\alpha^{2}+1\right)\cdot p+\left(\alpha-1\right)^{2}}{\alpha-1}\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> and </mtext><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\alpha\left(\alpha-1\right)}{\alpha+1}\leq p\text{ and }n\in\left(p\cdot\alpha+2\sqrt{p\cdot\alpha+p},\frac{\allowbreak\left(\alpha^{2}+1\right)\cdot p+\left(\alpha-1\right)^{2}}{\alpha-1}\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">then <math id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(G;x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(G;x)</annotation></semantics></math> is log-concave.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof.</span> If <math id="S3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=1</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is a complete graph, and its independence polynomial
is given by <math id="S3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1+nx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1+nx</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently, this polynomial is log-concave. Therefore,
we may assume that <math id="S3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>. By Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem8" title="Theorem 2.8 ‣ 2 Quasi-regularizability of 𝐖_𝑝 graphs ‣ Log-concavity of the independence polynomials of 𝐖_𝑝 graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.8</span></a>, <math id="S3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-quasi-regularizable, because <math id="S3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq(p+1)\cdot\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq(p+1)\cdot\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\in\mathbf{W}_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\in\mathbf{W}_{p}</annotation></semantics></math>. For all <math id="S3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq k\leq\alpha-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq k\leq\alpha-1</annotation></semantics></math>, Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma 3.2 ‣ 3 Log-concavity of independence polynomials of 𝐖_𝑝 graphs ‣ Log-concavity of the independence polynomials of 𝐖_𝑝 graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a> implies</p>
<table id="S3.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(k+1)\cdot s_{k+1}\leq(n-(p+1)\cdot k)\cdot s_{k},\text{ and }" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mtext> and </mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(k+1)\cdot s_{k+1}\leq(n-(p+1)\cdot k)\cdot s_{k},\text{ and }</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p\cdot(\alpha-k+1)\cdot s_{k-1}\leq k\cdot s_{k}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p\cdot(\alpha-k+1)\cdot s_{k-1}\leq k\cdot s_{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="S3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq(p+1)\cdot\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq(p+1)\cdot\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, then</p>
<table id="S3.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n-(p+1)\cdot k\geq n-(p+1)\cdot(\alpha-1)=n-(p+1)\cdot\alpha+p+1&gt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n-(p+1)\cdot k\geq n-(p+1)\cdot(\alpha-1)=n-(p+1)\cdot\alpha+p+1&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Hence,</p>
<table id="S3.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{k}^{2}\geq\frac{(k+1)\cdot p\cdot(\alpha-k+1)}{k\cdot(n-(p+1)\cdot k)}\cdot s_{k-1}\cdot s_{k+1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{k}^{2}\geq\frac{(k+1)\cdot p\cdot(\alpha-k+1)}{k\cdot(n-(p+1)\cdot k)}\cdot s_{k-1}\cdot s_{k+1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p3.4" class="ltx_p">We know that</p>
<table id="S3.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{(k+1)\cdot p\cdot(\alpha-k+1)}{k\cdot(n-(p+1)\cdot k)}\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{(k+1)\cdot p\cdot(\alpha-k+1)}{k\cdot(n-(p+1)\cdot k)}\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Leftrightarrow(k+1)\cdot p\cdot(\alpha-k+1)\geq k\cdot(n-(p+1)\cdot k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Leftrightarrow(k+1)\cdot p\cdot(\alpha-k+1)\geq k\cdot(n-(p+1)\cdot k)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Leftrightarrow k^{2}-(n-p\cdot\alpha)\cdot k+p\cdot\alpha+p\geq 0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Leftrightarrow k^{2}-(n-p\cdot\alpha)\cdot k+p\cdot\alpha+p\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p3.5" class="ltx_p">Now, we consider the function</p>
<table id="S3.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(k)=k^{2}-(n-p\cdot\alpha)\cdot k+p\cdot\alpha+p." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(k)=k^{2}-(n-p\cdot\alpha)\cdot k+p\cdot\alpha+p.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p3.6" class="ltx_p">Hence, its discriminant is</p>
<table id="S3.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=(n-p\cdot\alpha)^{2}-4\left(p\cdot\alpha+p\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=(n-p\cdot\alpha)^{2}-4\left(p\cdot\alpha+p\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Case 1</span>. <math id="S3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. This is equivalent to
<math id="S3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leq p\cdot\alpha+2\sqrt{p\cdot\alpha+p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leq p\cdot\alpha+2\sqrt{p\cdot\alpha+p}</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently, <math id="S3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(k)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(k)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> for
every <math id="S3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus <math id="S3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{k}^{2}\geq s_{k-1}\cdot s_{k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{k}^{2}\geq s_{k-1}\cdot s_{k+1}</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="S3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\left\{1,\ldots,\alpha-1\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\left\{1,\ldots,\alpha-1\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>, whenever</p>
<table id="S3.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(p+1\right)\cdot\alpha\leq n\leq p\cdot\alpha+2\sqrt{p\cdot\alpha+p}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(p+1\right)\cdot\alpha\leq n\leq p\cdot\alpha+2\sqrt{p\cdot\alpha+p}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Clearly, the set of integers <math id="S3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying the above constraints is not empty
if and only if <math id="S3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\alpha^{2}}{4\left(\alpha+1\right)}\leq p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\alpha^{2}}{4\left(\alpha+1\right)}\leq p</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Case 2</span>. <math id="S3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. This is equivalent to
<math id="S3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n&gt;p\cdot\alpha+2\sqrt{p\cdot\alpha+p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n&gt;p\cdot\alpha+2\sqrt{p\cdot\alpha+p}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, <math id="S3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(k)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(k)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> for every</p>
<table id="S3.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\leq k_{1}=\frac{n-p\cdot\alpha-\sqrt{\Delta}}{2}\text{ or }k\geq k_{2}=\frac{n-p\cdot\alpha+\sqrt{\Delta}}{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> or </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\leq k_{1}=\frac{n-p\cdot\alpha-\sqrt{\Delta}}{2}\text{ or }k\geq k_{2}=\frac{n-p\cdot\alpha+\sqrt{\Delta}}{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Subcase 2.1</span>. <math id="S3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha-1\leq k_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha-1\leq k_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p8.1" class="ltx_p">It means</p>
<table id="S3.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\alpha-1\leq\frac{n-p\cdot\alpha-\sqrt{\Delta}}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\alpha-1\leq\frac{n-p\cdot\alpha-\sqrt{\Delta}}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Leftrightarrow\sqrt{(n-p\cdot\alpha)^{2}-4\left(p\cdot\alpha+p\right)}\leq n-p\cdot\alpha-2\alpha+2," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Leftrightarrow\sqrt{(n-p\cdot\alpha)^{2}-4\left(p\cdot\alpha+p\right)}\leq n-p\cdot\alpha-2\alpha+2,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p8.2" class="ltx_p">which may be true if and only if <math id="S3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\cdot\alpha+2\alpha-2&lt;n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\cdot\alpha+2\alpha-2&lt;n</annotation></semantics></math>, since <math id="S3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
If this constraint is satisfied, then we may continue as follows:</p>
<table id="S3.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(n-p\cdot\alpha)^{2}-4\left(p\cdot\alpha+p\right)\leq\left(n-p\cdot\alpha-2\alpha+2\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(n-p\cdot\alpha)^{2}-4\left(p\cdot\alpha+p\right)\leq\left(n-p\cdot\alpha-2\alpha+2\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Leftrightarrow 0\leq 4n+4p-8\alpha-4n\alpha+4\alpha^{2}+4p\alpha^{2}+4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Leftrightarrow 0\leq 4n+4p-8\alpha-4n\alpha+4\alpha^{2}+4p\alpha^{2}+4</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Leftrightarrow n\leq\frac{\allowbreak\left(\alpha^{2}+1\right)\cdot p+\left(\alpha-1\right)^{2}}{\alpha-1}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Leftrightarrow n\leq\frac{\allowbreak\left(\alpha^{2}+1\right)\cdot p+\left(\alpha-1\right)^{2}}{\alpha-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p8.3" class="ltx_p">Thus <math id="S3.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{k}^{2}\geq s_{k-1}\cdot s_{k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{k}^{2}\geq s_{k-1}\cdot s_{k+1}</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="S3.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\left\{1,\ldots,\alpha-1\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\left\{1,\ldots,\alpha-1\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>, whenever</p>
<table id="S3.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta&gt;0\text{ and }\alpha\cdot\left(p+1\right)+\left(\alpha-1\right)\leq n\leq\frac{\allowbreak\left(\alpha^{2}+1\right)\cdot p+\left(\alpha-1\right)^{2}}{\alpha-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta&gt;0\text{ and }\alpha\cdot\left(p+1\right)+\left(\alpha-1\right)\leq n\leq\frac{\allowbreak\left(\alpha^{2}+1\right)\cdot p+\left(\alpha-1\right)^{2}}{\alpha-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p8.4" class="ltx_p">By the second constraint, if <math id="S3.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\alpha\left(\alpha-1\right)}{\alpha+1}&gt;p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\alpha\left(\alpha-1\right)}{\alpha+1}&gt;p</annotation></semantics></math>, then the set of integers <math id="S3.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying the above constraints is
empty. On the other hand, if <math id="S3.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\alpha\left(\alpha-1\right)}{\alpha+1}\leq p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\alpha\left(\alpha-1\right)}{\alpha+1}\leq p</annotation></semantics></math>, then</p>
<table id="S3.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\alpha\cdot\left(p+1\right)+\left(\alpha-2\right)\leq p\cdot\alpha+2\sqrt{p\cdot\alpha+p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\alpha\cdot\left(p+1\right)+\left(\alpha-2\right)\leq p\cdot\alpha+2\sqrt{p\cdot\alpha+p}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Leftrightarrow\alpha-1\leq\sqrt{p\cdot\alpha+p}\Leftrightarrow\alpha^{2}-2\alpha+1\leq p\cdot\alpha+p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Leftrightarrow\alpha-1\leq\sqrt{p\cdot\alpha+p}\Leftrightarrow\alpha^{2}-2\alpha+1\leq p\cdot\alpha+p</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p8.5" class="ltx_p">which is true, because</p>
<table id="S3.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\left(\alpha-1\right)^{2}}{\alpha+1}\leq\frac{\alpha\left(\alpha-1\right)}{\alpha+1}\leq p." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\left(\alpha-1\right)^{2}}{\alpha+1}\leq\frac{\alpha\left(\alpha-1\right)}{\alpha+1}\leq p.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p8.6" class="ltx_p">Thus <math id="S3.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{k}^{2}\geq s_{k-1}\cdot s_{k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{k}^{2}\geq s_{k-1}\cdot s_{k+1}</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="S3.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\left\{1,\ldots,\alpha-1\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\left\{1,\ldots,\alpha-1\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>, whenever</p>
<table id="S3.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p\cdot\alpha+2\sqrt{p\cdot\alpha+p}&lt;n\leq\frac{\allowbreak\left(\alpha^{2}+1\right)\cdot p+\left(\alpha-1\right)^{2}}{\alpha-1}\text{ and
}\frac{\alpha\left(\alpha-1\right)}{\alpha+1}\leq p." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mtext> and </mtext><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\cdot\alpha+2\sqrt{p\cdot\alpha+p}&lt;n\leq\frac{\allowbreak\left(\alpha^{2}+1\right)\cdot p+\left(\alpha-1\right)^{2}}{\alpha-1}\text{ and
}\frac{\alpha\left(\alpha-1\right)}{\alpha+1}\leq p.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Subcase 2.2</span>. <math id="S3.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{2}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{2}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p10.1" class="ltx_p">It means</p>
<table id="S3.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{n-p\cdot\alpha+\sqrt{(n-p\cdot\alpha)^{2}-4\left(p\cdot\alpha+p\right)}}{2}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{n-p\cdot\alpha+\sqrt{(n-p\cdot\alpha)^{2}-4\left(p\cdot\alpha+p\right)}}{2}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Leftrightarrow\sqrt{(n-p\cdot\alpha)^{2}-4\left(p\cdot\alpha+p\right)}\leq 2-n+p\alpha." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Leftrightarrow\sqrt{(n-p\cdot\alpha)^{2}-4\left(p\cdot\alpha+p\right)}\leq 2-n+p\alpha.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p11.1" class="ltx_p">It may be true if and only if <math id="S3.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n&lt;2+p\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n&lt;2+p\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, because <math id="S3.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. On the other
hand, the inequality <math id="S3.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(p+1\right)\cdot\alpha\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(p+1\right)\cdot\alpha\leq n</annotation></semantics></math> implies
<math id="S3.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=1</annotation></semantics></math>, which contradicts our assumption that <math id="S3.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p12.1" class="ltx_p">To conclude, it is worth mentioning that the inequality</p>
<table id="S3.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\cdot\alpha+2\sqrt{p\cdot\alpha+p}\leq\frac{\left(\alpha^{2}+1\right)\cdot p+(\alpha-1)^{2}}{\alpha-1}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\cdot\alpha+2\sqrt{p\cdot\alpha+p}\leq\frac{\left(\alpha^{2}+1\right)\cdot p+(\alpha-1)^{2}}{\alpha-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p12.2" class="ltx_p">is true, because it is equivalent to <math id="S3.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq\left(p+2\alpha+p\cdot\alpha-\alpha^{2}-1\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq\left(p+2\alpha+p\cdot\alpha-\alpha^{2}-1\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, if both <math id="S3.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S3.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\alpha\left(\alpha-1\right)}{\alpha+1}\leq p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\alpha\left(\alpha-1\right)}{\alpha+1}\leq p</annotation></semantics></math>, then</p>
<table id="S3.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p+2\alpha+p\alpha-\alpha^{2}-1\geq\frac{\alpha\left(\alpha-1\right)}{\alpha+1}+2\alpha+\frac{\alpha^{2}\left(\alpha-1\right)}{\alpha+1}-\alpha^{2}-1=\alpha-1&gt;0\text{.}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>.</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p+2\alpha+p\alpha-\alpha^{2}-1\geq\frac{\alpha\left(\alpha-1\right)}{\alpha+1}+2\alpha+\frac{\alpha^{2}\left(\alpha-1\right)}{\alpha+1}-\alpha^{2}-1=\alpha-1&gt;0\text{.}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p12.3" class="ltx_p">In other words, the interval <math id="S3.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left[\left(p+1\right)\cdot\alpha+\left(\alpha-1\right),\frac{\allowbreak\left(\alpha^{2}+1\right)\cdot p+\left(\alpha-1\right)^{2}}{\alpha-1}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left[\left(p+1\right)\cdot\alpha+\left(\alpha-1\right),\frac{\allowbreak\left(\alpha^{2}+1\right)\cdot p+\left(\alpha-1\right)^{2}}{\alpha-1}\right]</annotation></semantics></math> is not included in the
interval <math id="S3.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left[(p+1)\cdot\alpha,p\cdot\alpha+2\sqrt{p\cdot\alpha+p}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left[(p+1)\cdot\alpha,p\cdot\alpha+2\sqrt{p\cdot\alpha+p}\right]</annotation></semantics></math>.
 <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:5.0pt;height:5.0pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 3.4</span></span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> be a connected <math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> graph with <math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\neq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\neq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=n(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=n(G)</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=\alpha(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=\alpha(G)</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha-1\leq p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha-1\leq p</annotation></semantics></math> and</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p+1)\cdot\alpha\leq n\leq\frac{\allowbreak\left(\alpha^{2}+1\right)\cdot p+\left(\alpha-1\right)^{2}}{\alpha-1}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p+1)\cdot\alpha\leq n\leq\frac{\allowbreak\left(\alpha^{2}+1\right)\cdot p+\left(\alpha-1\right)^{2}}{\alpha-1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">then <math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(G;x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(G;x)</annotation></semantics></math> is log-concave.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p13.1" class="ltx_p">The graph <math id="S3.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{5}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is a <math id="S3.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> graph, illustrates that the
independence polynomial <math id="S3.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(G;x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(G;x)</annotation></semantics></math> can be log-concave even when <math id="S3.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p+1)\cdot\alpha(G)&gt;n(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p+1)\cdot\alpha(G)&gt;n(G)</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, note that <math id="S3.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(G;x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(G;x)</annotation></semantics></math> may remain log-concave even when
<math id="S3.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n(G)&gt;p\cdot\alpha(G)+2\sqrt{p\cdot\alpha+p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n(G)&gt;p\cdot\alpha(G)+2\sqrt{p\cdot\alpha+p}</annotation></semantics></math>. For instance, consider the
well-covered graphs <math id="S3.p13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.p13.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\geq 5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\geq 5</annotation></semantics></math> from Figure <a href="#S3.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 3 Log-concavity of independence polynomials of 𝐖_𝑝 graphs ‣ Log-concavity of the independence polynomials of 𝐖_𝑝 graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. It is clear
